Sub-agent code-review flow (goldenland-realestate-v2): use `delegate`/`reviewer` builtins — they inherit the session model and have shell access in the repo cwd (can run git); there is no specialized code-review subagent, so pass explicit shell diff instructions. If the user gives no fixed point for the code-review skill, pin it per-ticket from the commit graph (feature commit's parent SHA). For batched close-outs, run 2 axes × N tickets as parallel sub-agents (unlimited spawn budget). Trust nothing from the workflow completion event: aggregate returns get truncated and children fail with transient provider errors ('Model is unavailable') — inspect raw outputs in .pi-subagents/artifacts/ and re-run failed children. Before writing ledgers, verify findings against HEAD: later batch tickets may already fix them (e.g. #17/#18) — distinguish resolved-by-later-commit vs still-open-at-HEAD before assigning Fixed/Accepted dispositions. Delete dead code only when it has zero references at HEAD, excluding .pi-subagents/ and docs/agents/reviews/ artifacts. Ledgers go in docs/agents/reviews/<issue>.md: fixed point, spec source, standards sources, findings table (finding/axis/classification/disposition). <!-- created=2026-08-08, last=2026-08-08 -->